{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-65082","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124082","text":"stackdocs — specification"}]},{"id":"blk-65083","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124083","text":"What this system is, what it must do, what it must never do, and how to tell a correct implementation from a wrong one. Derived from the code at "},{"id":"spn-124084","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-124085","text":" in the ProjectAmp2 monorepo."}]},{"id":"blk-65084","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124086","text":"1. Purpose"}]},{"id":"blk-65085","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124087","text":"stackdocs produces a single self-contained HTML file ("},{"id":"spn-124088","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/index.html"},{"id":"spn-124089","text":") and a machine-readable sidecar ("},{"id":"spn-124090","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-124091","text":") that together mirror every documentation markdown file across the [&] monorepo as a navigable site. The site's routes are the source paths; an agent or a human can map between the two without a lookup table."}]},{"id":"blk-65086","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124092","text":"The build also produces one BendScript document per source file ("},{"id":"spn-124093","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/bend/*.bend.json"},{"id":"spn-124094","text":"), each validated and content-addressed."}]},{"id":"blk-65087","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124095","text":"2. Invariants"}]},{"id":"blk-65088","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124096","text":"These properties must hold on every successful build. A build that violates any of them must fail, not degrade."}]},{"id":"blk-65089","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124097","text":"2.1 Route-source identity"}]},{"id":"blk-65090","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124098","text":"For every page, "},{"id":"spn-124099","marks":["code"],"text":"route === source path"},{"id":"spn-124100","text":". The build must not move, rename, or re-root any file. A reader seeing route "},{"id":"spn-124101","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-124102","text":" must be able to open that exact path on disk."}]},{"id":"blk-65091","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124103","text":"2.2 BendScript validity"}]},{"id":"blk-65092","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124104","text":"Every page must be a valid BendScript document per the "},{"id":"spn-124105","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-124106","text":" schema. A document that cannot be validated degrades to a raw code-block view but is still validated in that form — it is never omitted."}]},{"id":"blk-65093","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124107","text":"2.3 Content-address fixpoint"}]},{"id":"blk-65094","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124108","text":"Every page is content-addressed (CIDv1). The round-trip "},{"id":"spn-124109","marks":["code"],"text":"parse(serialize(parse(doc)))"},{"id":"spn-124110","text":" must produce the same CID. This is checked across the entire corpus; a single violation fails the "},{"id":"spn-124111","marks":["code"],"text":"fixpointAll"},{"id":"spn-124112","text":" flag in the build report."}]},{"id":"blk-65095","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124113","text":"2.4 Build provenance"}]},{"id":"blk-65096","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124114","text":"Every build embeds a git commit hash as both a "},{"id":"spn-124115","marks":["code"],"text":"<meta name=\"build-commit\">"},{"id":"spn-124116","text":" tag and a field in the model JSON. The commit is derived from the latest non-"},{"id":"spn-124117","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-124118","text":" commit ("},{"id":"spn-124119","marks":["code"],"text":"git log -1 --format=%H -- . \":(exclude)dist\""},{"id":"spn-124120","text":"), not from HEAD. This is the \"two-commit chain\" strategy: source changes are committed first (the "},{"id":"spn-124121","marks":["italic"],"text":"source commit"},{"id":"spn-124122","text":"), then "},{"id":"spn-124123","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-124124","text":" is rebuilt and committed on top (the "},{"id":"spn-124125","marks":["italic"],"text":"artifact commit"},{"id":"spn-124126","text":"). The provenance always points to the source commit, breaking the self-referential cycle where committing "},{"id":"spn-124127","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-124128","text":" would change HEAD, which would change the embedded hash, which would require another commit."}]},{"id":"blk-65097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124129","text":"If no source commit can be resolved to a 40-hex-char SHA, the build fails. The build date is derived from the source commit's timestamp, not the wall clock, so that repeated builds of the same source commit produce byte-identical output regardless of when the artifact commit is made."}]},{"id":"blk-65098","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124130","text":"2.5 Derived facts, not literals"}]},{"id":"blk-65099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124131","text":"Canonical numbers (versions, law counts, trial counts) are read at build time from the file that owns them — "},{"id":"spn-124132","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-124133","text":" for npm versions, "},{"id":"spn-124134","marks":["code"],"text":"mix.exs"},{"id":"spn-124135","text":" for Elixir versions, the conformance harness source for law counts. A missing or unreadable source is a hard build failure. No fallback to a stale literal exists. The mechanism lives in "},{"id":"spn-124136","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124137","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-65100","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124138","text":"2.6 Cross-doc link integrity"}]},{"id":"blk-65101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124139","text":"Relative "},{"id":"spn-124140","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-124141","text":" links within the corpus that resolve to a known route become internal navigation edges. Unresolvable links degrade gracefully (they render as-is) but do not fail the build. The curated build ("},{"id":"spn-124142","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124143","text":") is stricter: a broken internal edge is a hard failure."}]},{"id":"blk-65102","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124144","text":"3. The dark factory"}]},{"id":"blk-65103","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124145","text":"The build derives a four-phase status model called the \"dark factory\" from "},{"id":"spn-124146","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-124147","text":". The four phases, in fixed order, are:"}]},{"id":"blk-65104","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65106","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124148","marks":["bold"],"text":"perceive"},{"id":"spn-124149","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-65105","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124150","marks":["bold"],"text":"decide"},{"id":"spn-124151","text":" — an explicit GAP (no step in §4 owns a decision-phase evidence rung)"}]}],"id":"blk-65107","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65110","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124152","marks":["bold"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-124153","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-65109","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124154","marks":["bold"],"text":"measure"},{"id":"spn-124155","text":" — sourced from §4 step 7"}]}],"id":"blk-65111","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-65113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124156","text":"Each sourced phase carries an evidence-ladder rung parsed from the owning table row. The valid rungs are: "},{"id":"spn-124157","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-124158","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124159","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-124160","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124161","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-124162","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124163","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-124164","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124165","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-124166","text":". A phase with no owning source is recorded as a named GAP with an explanatory string, not fabricated."}]},{"id":"blk-65114","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124167","text":"3.1 Dark-factory constraints"}]},{"id":"blk-65115","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124168","text":"The phase count must be exactly four, in the order above."}]}],"id":"blk-65116","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124169","text":"A GAP must not carry a rung or a source field."}]}],"id":"blk-65118","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65121","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124170","text":"The presentation layer ("},{"id":"spn-124171","marks":["code"],"text":"home.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124172","text":") must not contain any hard-coded evidence-rung literals ("},{"id":"spn-124173","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-124174","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124175","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-124176","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124177","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-124178","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124179","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-124180","text":"). The word "},{"id":"spn-124181","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-124182","text":" is allowed because it collides with the ship-status vocabulary; the unambiguous rung literals are the test boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-65120","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124183","text":"These constraints are enforced by "},{"id":"spn-124184","marks":["code"],"text":"test-dark-factory.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124185","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-124186","marks":["code"],"text":"npm test"},{"id":"spn-124187","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-65122","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-65124","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124188","text":"4. The verification gate"}]},{"id":"blk-65125","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124189","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-deployed.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124190","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-124191","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run verify:deployed"},{"id":"spn-124192","text":") is the gate for the docs reporting claim to reach "},{"id":"spn-124193","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-124194","text":". It:"}]},{"id":"blk-65126","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124195","text":"Fetches the production site at "},{"id":"spn-124196","marks":["code"],"text":"https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com"},{"id":"spn-124197","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-65127","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124198","text":"Extracts the embedded commit hash and model JSON."}]}],"id":"blk-65129","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65132","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124199","text":"Verifies internal consistency (meta tag commit === model commit)."}]}],"id":"blk-65131","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65134","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124200","text":"Checks that the local source commit (latest non-"},{"id":"spn-124201","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-124202","text":" commit) matches the production commit. Under the two-commit chain, this is the commit that produced the build, not HEAD."}]}],"id":"blk-65133","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124203","text":"Rebuilds locally from the same source."}]}],"id":"blk-65135","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65138","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124204","text":"Compares the dark-factory model field-by-field: phase order, rungs, sources, GAP status and text."}]}],"id":"blk-65137","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124205","text":"Checks that the production HTML contains visible references to "},{"id":"spn-124206","marks":["code"],"text":"darkFactory"},{"id":"spn-124207","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124208","marks":["code"],"text":"GAP"},{"id":"spn-124209","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-124210","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-124211","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-65139","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124212","text":"Fails if any divergence is found, including commit parity."}]}],"id":"blk-65141","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-65143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124213","text":"The script does not deploy. It only asserts that what is deployed matches what the source produces."}]},{"id":"blk-65144","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124214","text":"5. Deployment"}]},{"id":"blk-65145","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124215","text":"Deployment is a manual "},{"id":"spn-124216","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-docs.sh"},{"id":"spn-124217","text":" invocation that:"}]},{"id":"blk-65146","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124218","text":"Rebuilds the atlas from the live monorepo."}]}],"id":"blk-65147","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124219","text":"Clones the deploy repo ("},{"id":"spn-124220","marks":["code"],"text":"c-u-l8er/docs"},{"id":"spn-124221","text":") into a temp directory."}]}],"id":"blk-65149","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124222","text":"Mirrors "},{"id":"spn-124223","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-124224","text":" into the clone."}]}],"id":"blk-65151","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124225","text":"Commits and pushes only if something changed."}]}],"id":"blk-65153","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-65155","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124226","text":"Cloudflare Pages serves the deploy repo's "},{"id":"spn-124227","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-124228","text":" verbatim with no build step. The deploy repo is not this repo — it is a separate git repository that receives pre-built artifacts."}]},{"id":"blk-65156","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124229","text":"6. Two build modes"}]},{"id":"blk-65157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124230","text":"The codebase has two build pipelines:"}]},{"id":"blk-65158","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65160","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124231","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build-atlas.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-124232","text":" (primary, "},{"id":"spn-124233","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build"},{"id":"spn-124234","text":") — filesystem-mirror mode. Scans the entire monorepo, ingests every "},{"id":"spn-124235","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-124236","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-124237","marks":["code"],"text":"prompts/"},{"id":"spn-124238","text":" markdown file. Produces the homepage theme system (Runefort bands), the dark-factory model, and the atlas sidecar. This is what ships."}]}],"id":"blk-65159","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124239","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-124240","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-124241","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build:curated"},{"id":"spn-124242","text":") — curated mode. A hand-authored 21-page proof-of-concept defined entirely in "},{"id":"spn-124243","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124244","text":". Stricter link checking (broken internal edge = build failure). Supports transclusion ("},{"id":"spn-124245","marks":["code"],"text":"{{key}}"},{"id":"spn-124246","text":"). Does not scan the filesystem. Does not produce "},{"id":"spn-124247","marks":["code"],"text":"atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-124248","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-65161","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-65163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124249","text":"The reason for keeping both is not recorded in the code. The curated build appears to be the earlier prototype; the atlas build superseded it for production use."}]},{"id":"blk-65164","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124250","text":"7. Must-never-do"}]},{"id":"blk-65165","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124251","text":"Must never move, rename, or reorganize source files. The mirror property is load-bearing."}]}],"id":"blk-65166","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124252","text":"Must never hard-code a fact (version, count) that has a canonical source file. The derivation in "},{"id":"spn-124253","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124254","text":" is the only path."}]}],"id":"blk-65168","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124255","text":"Must never hard-code evidence-rung literals in the presentation layer."}]}],"id":"blk-65170","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124256","text":"Must never produce a deployment without a resolvable commit hash."}]}],"id":"blk-65172","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124257","text":"Must never silently succeed when a canonical source is missing or unreadable."}]}],"id":"blk-65174","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124258","text":"Must never fabricate a dark-factory rung or source for a phase that has no owning step."}]}],"id":"blk-65176","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-65178","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124259","text":"8. Dependencies"}]},{"id":"blk-65179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124260","text":"Two runtime dependencies, both from the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-65180","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124261","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-124262","text":" 0.1.0-alpha.0 — validation, content-addressing, serialization, parsing."}]}],"id":"blk-65181","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124263","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-124264","text":" 0.10.0 — imported by "},{"id":"spn-124265","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124266","text":" path traversal (law counting), not used as a runtime governance kernel in this codebase."}]}],"id":"blk-65183","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-65185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124267","text":"No other runtime dependencies. The build runs on Node.js with only built-in modules beyond these two."}]},{"id":"blk-65186","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124268","text":"9. Open questions"}]},{"id":"blk-65187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124269","text":"These are decisions the code makes whose reasons are not recorded:"}]},{"id":"blk-65188","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124270","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why keep the curated build?"},{"id":"spn-124271","text":" "},{"id":"spn-124272","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124273","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-124274","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124275","text":" are a complete second pipeline with hand-authored content. The atlas build superseded it for production. Whether the curated build is still exercised, depended on, or slated for removal is not stated."}]}],"id":"blk-65189","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124276","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why does `box-and-box` appear in `package.json`?"},{"id":"spn-124277","text":" It is listed as a dependency but "},{"id":"spn-124278","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-124279","text":" reads from the monorepo path "},{"id":"spn-124280","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/"},{"id":"spn-124281","text":", not from "},{"id":"spn-124282","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules"},{"id":"spn-124283","text":". The installed package may be unused. The reason for its inclusion is not recorded."}]}],"id":"blk-65191","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-65194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124284","marks":["bold"],"text":"Fallback-vs-failure asymmetry."},{"id":"spn-124285","text":" The atlas build treats an unparseable document as a graceful fallback (raw code block); the curated build treats a broken internal edge as a hard failure. Both are defensible but the difference in failure philosophy is not explained."}]}],"id":"blk-65193","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-65195","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-124286","text":"10. What is already written down elsewhere"}]},{"id":"blk-65196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124287","text":"The referenced ADR documents ("},{"id":"spn-124288","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0004"},{"id":"spn-124289","text":" through "},{"id":"spn-124290","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0008"},{"id":"spn-124291","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124292","marks":["code"],"text":"SUPERVISOR.md"},{"id":"spn-124293","text":", "},{"id":"spn-124294","marks":["code"],"text":"workbench spec"},{"id":"spn-124295","text":") are about WebHost.Systems and the workbench, not about this codebase. They share vocabulary (deployment immutability, provenance, telemetry) but do not describe stackdocs. The "},{"id":"spn-124296","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"},{"id":"spn-124297","text":" in this directory is the closest thing to a prior spec; this document supersedes it for normative purposes."}]},{"id":"blk-65197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-124298","text":"No design document for this codebase existed before this file."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera7ohytqilwswin6dsf6misq5fvwdfrqx4huzltt7gfegsaks6agja","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}